 "about": "Rules for tiering new-ingredient proposals during external-site batch reviews (nyt_work/tier.py). Auto = applied without asking (listed in a skim file); Confirm = one table, silence means yes; Ask = needs the user's call. Every correction the user makes becomes a word below or a case in 'cases'; tier.py --backtest checks no case ever lands in Auto. Default words (fresh, whole, ripe, raw) are neutral: only the MARKED form (dried, ground, underripe...) makes a different product. A capitalised word counts as a possible variety/brand only if the master never uses it as an ordinary lowercase word (so 'Garlic croutons' is not flagged).",
