 "standing_rulings": [
  "Low-fat / reduced-fat / nonfat / skim / 1% / 2% milk, yogurt, sour cream, cottage cheese, ricotta, cream cheese -> the regular product (parser rule, not evaporated/condensed).",
  "A different variety, ripeness, or form (ground vs whole, dried vs fresh, hot vs sweet, smoked, roe) gets its own entry; nutrition may stand in for the base product.",
  "Generic pasta shapes -> pasta; most blue cheeses -> blue cheese; rich/well-seasoned broths -> chicken broth; veal bones -> beef bones; fruity red wine is NOT dry red wine.",
  "Prep in a wording (precooked, dried and crumbled, cleaned and split, rinsed and boned) becomes a Prep step: the name stays the bought product.",
  "Brand-dependent restrictions (verjus sulfite, baking powder sulfite) = none; restrictions err conservative otherwise.",
  "Never merge away a Mealime-sourced id.",
  "Snails (escargot) count as shellfish [4].",
  "Cooking by-products (pasta cooking water) are not ingredients: a 'note' override row, no entry, no restriction.",
  "A regional cheese that differs from its stand-in in key aspects gets its own entry (anthotyro is not ricotta); almond macaroons are not amaretti; Melba toast is its own product.",
  "Any prep inside an override name (pureed, melted, toasted and buttered, steeped) must come out as a Prep sentence: check it with prepcheck after the re-align.",
  "Paprika: sweet (the 'paprika' entry), hot, smoked and hot smoked are separate entries with the same nutrition (different culinary use).",
  "A distinct type of grain gets its own entry even when a close one exists (black glutinous rice is not forbidden black rice).",
  "Semolina and cornmeal are different products: never merge one into the other.",
  "Roasted oils (roasted walnut oil) are a different product from the plain oil; roasted/salted nuts and seeds are not (they join the plain entry).",
  "Generic 'X fruit' wordings go to a generic mixed entry (freeze-dried mixed fruit), not to one example fruit.",
  "Any prep word inside a wording (slivered, steamed, well-cooked, ground, slant-cut) must survive as a Prep sentence: write an override row, never a bare join.",
  "No-salt-added / low-sodium versions are their own entries (they matter to a recipe's flavor), e.g. 'diced tomatoes, no salt added'. Batch 8 ruling; older merges of no-salt wordings may need revisiting.",
  "Lower-fat dairy rule extends to evaporated skim milk -> evaporated milk and reduced-fat goat cheese -> goat cheese.",
  "'X or Y' where Y is a close cousin: take the simpler, common one (mackerel or sardines -> sardines).",
  "Plant-based meat substitutes -> the existing 'veggie ground, plant based' entry."
 ],
